<title>USA: Amax Gold files $200 mln shelf with SEC.</title>
<headline>Amax Gold files $200 mln shelf with SEC.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Amax Gold Inc filed a shelf registration statement with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission to offer up to $200 million in debt, stock and warrants.</p>
<p>The company said it may offer debt securities, preferred stock, common stock and warrants to buy debt, preferred and common shares.</p>
<p>The company intends to use the proceeds to repay debt, finance operations for the continued development of its gold projects and for other general corporate purposes, the filing said.</p>
</text>
